course: dictionary
lesson: 8553
title: One word, many meanings: scan
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word scan has more than one meaning, so you must use the context to know which one is meant. The words around it are the clues. «Scan the page for the date» means look quickly to find one thing. «Scan the horizon» means look carefully all around.
explain: Scan can be a verb (an action) or a noun (a thing). In «At a self-checkout you scan your own shopping», someone is doing the action, so it is a verb. In «an ultrasound scan», the scan is a medical picture made by a machine, so it is a noun. Ask yourself: is someone doing something, or is it a thing?
explain: In reading lessons, scanning is a skill: moving your eyes quickly to find a key word, name or number. Skimming is different, because it gets the main idea. When you hunt for one fact, scan. When you want the big picture, skim. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
fact: Scan can be a verb (scan, scans, scanned, scanning) or a noun (a scan, scans).
fact: «Scan» means to look quickly over something to find a particular piece of information.
fact: «Scan» also means to look carefully all around an area, as in «scan the room».
fact: To scan a picture or document means to copy it into a computer using a machine called a scanner.
fact: A scan is a medical picture of the inside of the body, made by a machine, such as «a baby scan».
exercise: «Scan the page for the date.» What does scan mean here? | To sing loudly and clearly | *To look quickly over something to find one piece of information | To draw a picture of the page | To fold the page neatly in half
exercise: «The doctor looked at the scan.» What kind of word is scan in this sentence? | *A noun, a thing | An adjective, a describing word | A question word | A verb, an action
exercise: «Scan the horizon for ships.» What does scan the horizon suggest? | Go to sleep | *Look carefully all around | Copy a document into a computer | Read the price on a label
test: «The cashier scanned my bag.» What does scanned mean here? | Sold the bag to a friend | Lost the bag on the bus | Painted the bag bright blue | *Read the barcodes with a machine
test: Which one describes scanning as a reading skill? | Drawing pictures of the main ideas | Reading every line slowly to enjoy the story | *Moving your eyes quickly to find a key word, name or number | Listening to someone read aloud
exam: Which sentence uses scan to mean looking quickly for one key fact? | The doctor booked a scan for Tuesday | The machine made a copy of my drawing | The shop worker scanned the barcode | *Mum scanned the list for my name
